    <string name="lesson_tap_title">Tap an arrow</string>
    <string name="lesson_tap_body">Each arrow slides where it points and leaves over the edge. These three have a clear way out.</string>
    <string name="lesson_blocking_title">Blocking</string>
    <string name="lesson_blocking_body">If another arrow is in the way it cannot leave, and you lose a life. Take out the one in the way first.</string>
    <string name="lesson_chain_title">Chains</string>
    <string name="lesson_chain_body">Taking out an arrow frees the one behind it. Find where the row starts.</string>
    <string name="lesson_long_title">Long arrows</string>
    <string name="lesson_long_body">A long arrow fills a whole line until it leaves. Only what is in front of its tip matters.</string>
    <string name="lesson_bent_title">Bent arrows</string>
    <string name="lesson_bent_body">They move like a snake: the tail follows the head. When they leave, their cells are free.</string>
    <string name="lesson_traveler_title">Travelers</string>
    <string name="lesson_traveler_body">Travelers fold over the edge and go on along the next face. Check that face too before tapping.</string>
    <string name="lesson_combo_title">Combos</string>
    <string name="lesson_combo_body">Take arrows out one after another, fast and without mistakes: each one multiplies your points. Tapping a blocked one breaks the combo.</string>
